from pathlib import Path
p=Path('build_report.py')
s=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8')
s=s.replace("g('sm_age.Age<30.n')", "g('sm_selfemp.Age<30.n')")
s=s.replace("g('sm_age.Age>=30.n')", "g('sm_selfemp.Age>=30.n')")
s=s.replace("g('sm_age.Full.n')", "g('sm_selfemp.Full.n')")
s=s.replace("They encode different decision policies.", "They encode different decision policies. That distinction matters because a score is not itself a policy. The analyst still chooses the cut point, decides which errors are acceptable, and determines whether a person receives review or an automatic outcome.")
s=s.replace("The important result is not that one reduced model is the truth.", "The important result is not that one reduced model is the truth; it is that the coefficient depends on the feature set and can move materially when a plausible predictor is removed.")
s=s.replace("A responsible audit should ask why this pocket exists and whether the same pattern appears in a new cohort before changing the deployment threshold.", "A responsible audit should ask why this pocket exists and whether the same pattern appears in a new cohort before changing the deployment threshold. I would also document the review criteria so the error analysis remains reproducible rather than anecdotal.")
s=s.replace("These are not reasons to throw the model away; they are reasons to treat the model as one piece of evidence and to publish the limits alongside the score.", "These are not reasons to throw the model away; they are reasons to treat the model as one piece of evidence and to publish the limits alongside the score. The model score is also conditional on the dataset, preprocessing pipeline and target definition. If data collection changes, the threshold may not have the same meaning. I would track subgroup confusion matrices over time and separate model monitoring from policy monitoring. Finally, I would keep an appeal path so people affected by a high-stakes prediction can provide missing information or request human reconsideration. Responsible evaluation is model, threshold, data context and human process, not model accuracy alone.")
s=s.replace("I also checked the Male-only subgroup issue: the Male group has {R['male_relationship_wife_count']['full']} rows with relationship_Wife in the full data, so the Wife dummy is degenerate there. I therefore do not claim a Wife coefficient reversal inside the Male subgroup.", "I also checked the Male+Wife count: the Male group has {R['male_relationship_wife_count']['full']} such rows in the full data. That makes the category rare rather than absent, so I do not claim a separate within-Male coefficient reversal from this small cell. The key point is the matched-pair offset, not a direct sex penalty.")
p.write_text(s,encoding='utf-8')
print('Patched build_report.py report checks and final reflection length')
